// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CALIBRATION[pathogen] = [{ closeShare, G, emissionMedian, achieved }]
// For each target close-range share (close / (close + room) among infections
// acquired in the building, no lamps), the (G, emission.median) pair at which
// the no-lamp baseline reproduces that share and the pathogen's attack-rate
// target, all other parameters at their defaults. Regenerate with
//   node src/cli.js calibrate --write
// The block between the markers is machine-written.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CALIBRATION-BEGIN
// covid: refitted 2026-11-11 (fourth pass), 200 season seeds per evaluation (seeds 1-200), at unreachable shares 0.1, 0.24, 0.4, 0.55, 0.7
//   and 0.86 (the scenario values 0.24 / 0.55 / 0.86 are fitted rows, so no scenario interpolates or extrapolates). "closeShare" is the
//   share of in-home infections that room-air cleaning cannot reach; in the model all of it travels by the face-to-face route (hands and
//   surfaces are not simulated separately). Three free quantities per share: emission median, G, staff community hazard (visitor
//   infectiousness = 6 × hazard). Targets: season resident incidence 0.1874 (Franklin et al. 2024, MMWR: 109.3 per 10,000 resident-weeks
//   × 120 days), median facility-outbreak resident attack rate 0.21 (Rodríguez Campelo et al. 2023; outbreaks = cases incl. staff, new
//   outbreak after 14 days without a case, ≥ 2 resident cases), and the share. The outbreak median is a noisy statistic of a two-humped
//   distribution: rows land between 0.17 and 0.22 (0.55 row: 0.17). Mask compliance 0.7.
// flu, rsv rows are from the second pass, when the share meant only the face-to-face part of airborne spread.
// flu, rsv: NOT VALIDATED. Fitted 2026-11-11 to median reported-outbreak attack rates (flu 0.33, Lansbury 2017; RSV 0.24, Osei-Yeboah 2024) with
//   300 single-introduction runs; they need emission far above the literature and give implausible season attack rates (flu ~57%, RSV ~41%). Do not publish.
